{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"perkish-balsamic-pupfish","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## What happened\n\nA story that was legitimately SUPERSEDED cannot be closed by any non-`--force` path, because two\nmechanisms contradict each other:\n\n1. `rebar transition <id> open closed --class=superseded`, with a **live `supersedes` link**\n   already recorded, is refused:\n\n   > `plan-review close gate: unsigned: no certified plan-review attestation. Run rebar\n   > review-plan <id> separately, then retry close.`\n\n2. `rebar review-plan <id>` on that same ticket **cannot pass** — and correctly so. The reviewer\n   returns BLOCK with three critical `G1G2` findings whose substance is *\"the described edit\n   target content does not exist / the test you plan to write already exists\"*:\n\n   > \"The guide lines the plan names as needing cut-over already contain `[non-codebase]` …\"\n   > \"that test already asserts `[non-codebase]` is present\"\n   > \"AC4's 'NEW negative test' already exists as `test_legacy_alias_stays_undocumented`\"\n\nThat is precisely what \"superseded\" MEANS: another change already delivered this plan's work. The\ngate demands an attestation that the ticket is, by construction, unable to earn — the more\ncorrectly it is superseded, the more certainly its review blocks.\n\n## Why the existing escape does not cover it\n\n`rebar transition --help` states that an administrative disposition skips **completion\nverification** when its evidence holds (a live `duplicates`/`supersedes` link, or a required\nclose reason). That evidence was present here. But the skip does not extend to the **plan-review\nclose gate** (`require_plan_review_for_close`), which still demands a certified attestation, so\nthe administrative path is blocked anyway.\n\nThe only remaining route is `--force=<reason>`, which AGENTS.md explicitly reserves for a human\noperator's judgment call and which deliberately records **no signed attestation**. So every\nsuperseded ticket permanently degrades the audit trail, for a disposition that is administrative\nand evidence-backed rather than a bypass of real verification.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n1. Create stories A and B; give B a plan whose work A will absorb.\n2. Land A, implementing everything B planned.\n3. `rebar link A B supersedes` (evidence for the administrative disposition).\n4. `rebar transition B open closed --class=superseded` → refused, `plan-review close gate: unsigned`.\n5. `rebar review-plan B` → BLOCK, findings all of the form \"this work already exists\".\n6. Goto 4. There is no non-`--force` exit.\n\n## Suggested direction (not a prescription)\n\nThe administrative dispositions that already skip completion verification on live-link evidence\n(`superseded`, `duplicate`) are candidates for skipping the plan-review close gate on the SAME\nevidence. The gate exists to certify that work about to be done, or just done, was reviewed —\nneither applies to a ticket whose work was delivered elsewhere and which is being closed as a\nbookkeeping act.\n\n`obsolete`/`wontfix` (reason-required rather than link-backed) may warrant different treatment;\nthis ticket is only about the link-backed dispositions.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A ticket with a live `supersedes` (or `duplicates`) link can be closed under its matching\n      `--class` without `--force` and without a plan-review attestation.\n- [ ] The close still refuses when the claimed evidence is absent — no live link means no skip.\n- [ ] The resulting close is distinguishable in the audit trail from a `--force` close (it is an\n      evidence-backed disposition, not an unaudited bypass).\n- [ ] A test drives the six-step reproduction above and asserts step 4 succeeds.","id":"69b9-b740-c53a-4b56","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Superseded tickets cannot be closed: plan-review close gate demands an attestation they cannot earn"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787253524642113001,"uuid":"b2ca7d51-9a25-4da9-adff-da0f6b49a19b"}